  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "acf",
      "name": "acf/block-full-bg-image",
      "anchor": "about-conf",
      "data": {
        "block_title": null,
        "block_description": "<p class=\"font-montserrat mb-0\" style=\"font-size: 120%; line-height: 170%; font-weight: 400; text-align: left;\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">The 2022 edition centers on connecting and inspiring. Let's dive into the latest challenges &amp; opportunities in building modern software systems. Reconnect with tech experts at the 100% offline event hosted in Krakow's Manggha Museum. </span></p>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<p class=\"font-montserrat mb-0\" style=\"font-size: 120%; line-height: 170%; font-weight: 400; text-align: left;\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Get ready for an interdisciplinary program delivered by professionals from cloud-native architectures, data engineering &amp; data science, developer tooling, frontend engineering, and UX area.</span></p>",
        "block_button": null,
        "cta_background_color": null,
        "cta_font_color": null,
        "cta_border_radius": null,
        "block_background_image": null,
        "block_background_color": "#e9e4e0",
        "block_font_color": "#0c1e19",
        "menu_label": "About"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "acf",
      "name": "acf/block-conf-2022-agenda",
      "anchor": "acf-block-634941266dc22",
      "data": {
        "block_title": "Conference schedule",
        "block_agenda": [
          {
            "label": "Day 1 - Tuesday, 20.09",
            "day_schedule": [
              {
                "item_type": "other",
                "start_time": "17:00:00",
                "end_time": "18:00:00",
                "selected_talk": null,
                "is_keynote": false,
                "link_talk": false,
                "talk_summary": null,
                "item_title": "Registration",
                "icon": null
              },
              {
                "item_type": "other",
                "start_time": "18:00:00",
                "end_time": null,
                "selected_talk": null,
                "is_keynote": false,
                "link_talk": false,
                "talk_summary": null,
                "item_title": "Event opening",
                "icon": null
              },
              {
                "item_type": "talk",
                "start_time": "18:15:00",
                "end_time": "18:35:00",
                "selected_talk": 3239,
                "is_keynote": false,
                "link_talk": false,
                "talk_summary": "Recently I’ve made a little experiment trying to create a clone of the Space Invaders game not writing a single line of code. I employed Github Copilot AI to do it. It kind of worked but also filled my head with ideas. How did it work? Will AI take developers' jobs soon? Are we all doomed?\r\n",
                "item_title": null,
                "icon": null
              },
              {
                "item_type": "talk",
                "start_time": "18:45:00",
                "end_time": "19:05:00",
                "selected_talk": 3249,
                "is_keynote": false,
                "link_talk": false,
                "talk_summary": null,
                "item_title": null,
                "icon": null
              },
              {
                "item_type": "other",
                "start_time": "19:05:00",
                "end_time": null,
                "selected_talk": null,
                "is_keynote": false,
                "link_talk": false,
                "talk_summary": null,
                "item_title": "<small>15-minute break</small>",
                "icon": {
                  "id": 3206,
                  "url": "/uploads/2022/04/icon_coffee.png",
                  "alt": "Coffee icon",
                  "width": 55,
                  "height": 54
                }
              },
              {
                "item_type": "talk",
                "start_time": "19:20:00",
                "end_time": "19:40:00",
                "selected_talk": 3233,
                "is_keynote": false,
                "link_talk": false,
                "talk_summary": "Dumping all your code into a single shared monorepository is all the rage. But our tooling is only catching up with the new paradigm. \r\n\r\nWe'll go over how large repositories and common patterns in them are breaking long-standing assumptions in IntelliJ IDEA in terms of project model, performance, and user experience. Then we will take a look at our current ideas and approaches to solving these problems in a monorepo world.",
                "item_title": null,
                "icon": null
              },
              {
                "item_type": "talk",
                "start_time": "19:50:00",
                "end_time": "20:30:00",
                "selected_talk": 3287,
                "is_keynote": true,
                "link_talk": false,
                "talk_summary": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\r\n<p>The Economic Progression Model proposed by Joseph Pine and James Gilmore depicts the economic development in the Western world as it is happening in front of our eyes. From one stance, you can say that the final stage: transformational experience is the natural end of the proposed progression. </p>\r\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\r\n\r\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\r\n<p>From another stance, though, we may consider it an end to a certain phase of economic progress and an opening to a new perspective - delivering value. Such value goes beyond the monetary gain and encapsulates the broad range of change we want to see in the world. Through my presentation, I would like to invite you to a discussion on how experience design could elevate transformative change through contributions that positively impact the world in the direction we hope for.</p>\r\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
                "item_title": null,
                "icon": null
              },
              {
                "item_type": "other",
                "start_time": "20:30:00",
                "end_time": "02:00:00",
                "selected_talk": null,
                "is_keynote": false,
                "link_talk": false,
                "talk_summary": null,
                "item_title": "Afterparty",
                "icon": {
                  "id": 3207,
                  "url": "/uploads/2022/04/icon_glasses.png",
                  "alt": "Glasses icon",
                  "width": 60,
                  "height": 74
                }
              }
            ],
            "add_load_more_button": false,
            "show_more_index": null
